    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Merin Joji<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Thursday, June 20, 2024 4:26 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> geomorph R package &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] Session Abort error while running gm.prcomp to map phylomorphospace<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dear Geomorph,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I have been trying to map the turtle phylogeny tree and coordinates to phylomorphospace; it does not show any error but shows\r\n<b>R session aborted (ss).</b> I tried on both Windows and Mac, all having the latest version of R and Geomorph. Below is the code I used; if needed, I can also share my data files privately. Anyone facing issues while plotting phylogeny? Thank you for helping.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1d1c1d;background:#f8f8f8\">###Read phylogeny###library(xml2)</span><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1d1c1d\"><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">library(geomorph)</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">library(geiger)</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">library(ape)</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">library(ggplot2)</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">library(phytools)</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">library(Morpho)setwd(&quot;D:/ADMIN/Documents/University of copenhagen docs/Testudines_museum_data&quot;)</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">sliders&lt;- read.csv(&quot;curves_slider_matrix.csv&quot;, sep=&quot;;&quot;, header=FALSE)</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">tt_ref1 &lt;- read.csv(&quot;JMP_Shape means_Merin&amp;Laura.csv&quot;, sep=&quot;,&quot;, header=TRUE, row.names = 1)</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">Tree&lt;- read.nexus(&quot;Merin_figtree.nex&quot;)</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">tt_ref1 &lt;- arrayspecs(tt_ref1, 265, 3)T.gpa_ref1&lt;- gpagen(tt_ref1, curves = sliders)</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">Y.gpa_ref1&lt;- gpagen(T.gpa_ref1$coords, print.progress = FALSE)Csize&lt;- T.gpa_ref1$Csize</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">shape &lt;- Y.gpa_ref1$coords</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">ecology&lt;- read.csv(&quot;Ecology_Merin&amp;Laura.csv&quot;, header = TRUE, row.names=1)shape.test &lt;- treedata(phy = Tree, data = two.d.array(shape), warnings = TRUE)</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">data.matched &lt;- treedata(phy = Tree, data = ecology, warnings= FALSE)</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">elev &lt;- as.factor(data.matched$data); names(elev) &lt;- row.names(data.matched$data)</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">gdf &lt;- geomorph.data.frame(shape=shape, shape = shape,elev = elev, Tree = Tree$`&#39;Merin_figtree&#39;`)</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">#Phylomorphospace - PCA with phylogeny</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">#Estimated ancestral states projected to the plot</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">plot.pca &lt;- gm.prcomp(shape,phy= Tree) ### R IS CRASHING###</span><br>\r\n<span style=\"background:#f8f8f8\">plot(plot.pca,phylo = TRUE, pch=21, bg=gdf$elev, cex=2, phylo.par = list(tip.labels = FALSE, node.labels = FALSE) )summary(plot.pca)</span></span><u></u><u></u